# Neon Database Migration Configuration
# This file documents the Neon connection strings for all environments
# 
# DO NOT commit actual connection strings to version control
# Store real connection strings in:
# - .env (gitignored) for development
# - Kubernetes secrets for staging/production
# - Environment variables in CI/CD for deployments

# ============================================
# DEVELOPMENT BRANCH (Development Environment)
# ============================================
# Scale-to-zero after 5 minutes inactivity
# Fastest resume time: ~1-5 seconds
# Best for: Local development, feature testing
#
# Replace with actual Neon dev branch connection string:
# Example format: postgresql://neondb:password@ep-dev-xxxxx.us-east-1.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require
#
DATABASE_URL_DEV=postgresql://neondb:PASSWORD@ep-dev-XXXXX.us-east-1.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require

# ============================================
# STAGING BRANCH (Staging Environment)
# ============================================
# Autoscaling: 0.5-1 CU
# Peak hours: 06:00-22:00 UTC (1 CU)
# Off-peak: 22:00-06:00 UTC (0.5 CU)
# Best for: Integration testing, pre-production validation
#
# Replace with actual Neon staging branch connection string:
# Example format: postgresql://neondb:password@ep-staging-xxxxx.us-east-1.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require
#
DATABASE_URL_STAGING=postgresql://neondb:PASSWORD@ep-staging-XXXXX.us-east-1.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require

# ============================================
# PRODUCTION BRANCH (Production Environment)
# ============================================
# Fixed 1 CU compute (no autoscaling)
# Always-on for maximum availability
# Best for: Live user traffic, production data
#
# Replace with actual Neon production branch connection string:
# Example format: postgresql://neondb:password@ep-prod-xxxxx.us-east-1.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require
#
DATABASE_URL_PROD=postgresql://neondb:PASSWORD@ep-prod-XXXXX.us-east-1.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require

# ============================================
# SETUP INSTRUCTIONS
# ============================================
#
# 1. Create Neon account at https://console.neon.tech
#
# 2. Create project "bank-api-prod" in region us-east-1
#
# 3. Create three branches:
#    - production (parent: main)
#    - staging (parent: production)
#    - development (parent: staging)
#
# 4. Get connection strings:
#    neonctl connection-string --project-id proj-xxxxx --branch-name development
#    neonctl connection-string --project-id proj-xxxxx --branch-name staging
#    neonctl connection-string --project-id proj-xxxxx --branch-name production
#
# 5. Update this file with actual connection strings
#
# 6. For development:
#    - Copy DATABASE_URL_DEV to .env DATABASE_URL variable
#    - Keep .env in .gitignore
#
# 7. For staging/production:
#    - Store connection strings in Kubernetes secrets:
#      kubectl create secret generic neon-staging-db --from-literal=connection-string='...' --namespace=staging
#      kubectl create secret generic neon-prod-db --from-literal=connection-string='...' --namespace=production

# ============================================
# NEON CLI COMMANDS
# ============================================
#
# Install Neon CLI:
# npm install -g neonctl
#
# Login to Neon:
# neonctl auth
#
# List projects:
# neonctl projects list
#
# Create project:
# neonctl projects create --name bank-api-prod --region us-east-1
#
# Create branch:
# neonctl branches create --project-id proj-xxxxx --branch-name development --parent staging
#
# Get connection string:
# neonctl connection-string --project-id proj-xxxxx --branch-name development
#
# List branches:
# neonctl branches list --project-id proj-xxxxx

# ============================================
# SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS
# ============================================
#
# - Connection strings contain credentials, handle carefully
# - Never commit real connection strings to version control
# - Rotate credentials regularly (through Neon console)
# - Use environment variables in CI/CD pipelines
# - Restrict .env file permissions: chmod 600 .env
# - Use Kubernetes secrets for containerized deployments

# ============================================
# NEON FEATURES FOR THIS PROJECT
# ============================================
#
# Development:
# - Scale-to-zero: Automatically suspends after 5 minutes inactivity
# - Cost: ~$5/month
# - Useful for: Development, testing, reducing costs
#
# Staging:
# - Autoscaling: Automatically scales between 0.5-1 CU based on demand
# - Cost: ~$20/month
# - Useful for: Pre-production validation with realistic scaling
#
# Production:
# - Fixed compute: 1 CU always available for consistent performance
# - Cost: ~$100/month
# - Useful for: Live user traffic, predictable performance
#
# Total monthly cost: ~$125 (saves ~$75/month vs. dedicated server)

# ============================================
# MIGRATION TIMELINE
# ============================================
#
# Phase 1 (Week 1): Pre-migration setup
# - Create Neon project and branches ← You are here
# - Update EF Core configuration
# - Prepare source database
#
# Phase 2 (Week 2): Schema migration
# - Run EF Core migrations to all three branches
# - Verify schema integrity
#
# Phase 3 (Week 3): Data migration
# - Bulk copy data from source to Neon
# - Validate row counts and integrity
#
# Phase 4 (Week 4): Configuration updates
# - Update Docker Compose
# - Update Kubernetes manifests
# - Update Terraform
#
# Phase 5 (Week 5): Production cutover
# - Execute dry-run on staging
# - Execute production cutover (Sunday 02:00 UTC)
#
# Phase 6 (Week 6+): Post-migration
# - Run smoke tests
# - Monitor performance
# - Optimize costs

